# Heavy binary artefacts go through Git LFS. Currently this covers the
# WASM clang+lld toolchain bundle under web/assets/emception/ — built
# locally via web/lib/build-toolchain.sh.
#
# Background: the CI workflow that used to produce this bundle
# (.github/workflows/build-llvm-box-arm.yml) was deleted. The cold-
# cache LLVM + Emscripten build runs roughly 3 hours, and the multi-
# gigabyte intermediate state doesn't cache cleanly between runs.
# Maintaining a runner image for it is more friction than just
# rebuilding locally on the rare occasion the toolchain needs a bump,
# then committing the output via Git LFS.
#
# To rebuild from scratch: read the header of web/lib/build-toolchain.sh
# (covers emsdk 3.1.24 pin, the ARM-target patch, the cmake 3.24 pin
# for Emception's patch-ninja regex, and the macOS-vs-Linux PATH
# tweaks). Run it, then `git add web/assets/emception/` — LFS picks
# up the *.wasm and *.pack.br files automatically per the rules below.
*.wasm    filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.pack.br filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.pack    filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
